   137	```text
   138	{type: "transition", from_step: t, actions: [seat0, seat1],
   139	 expected: post_transition_public, privates: post_transition_privates,
   140	 statuses: [seat0, seat1], rewards: [seat0, seat1]}
   141	```
   142	
   143	The native CLI does **not** read this gzip/JSONL representation directly. Its
   144	`ReplayInput` is one JSON object `{header, transitions: [{actions}, ...]}`.
   145	It emits one `StepSnapshot` per initial/successor state:
   146	`{public, privates, done, statuses, rewards}`. The JSONL oracle's `expected` maps
   147	to snapshot `public`; `done` is checked separately. `type`/`source` are fixture
   148	metadata beyond the typed native header. Native `TraceHeader` still requires
   149	the schedule, initial, terminal-bank and count fields, even though several are
   150	not used to construct a game.
   151	
   152	`Game::from_seed_header` validates the format/configuration/player counts, creates
   153	the standard initial state from configuration, and sets the resolved seed. It
   154	does **not** load the supplied initial state, RNG schedule, shop schedule or final
   155	banks as answers. `Game::from_header` loads an explicit state and therefore cannot
   156	prove a seed-header round trip. The schedules can be empty in a newly generated
   157	native header; if recorded as diagnostics, their provenance must be explicit.
   158	
   159	All four fixtures contain 29 `rng_schedule` records with 200 rolls each. These
   160	are legacy diagnostic schedules, not a promise that the engine consumes 200 draws:
   161	`end_of_day` only draws for null tiles, in seat/y/x order, then draws a shop when
   162	eligible. It reinitializes Python-compatible RNG each day with
   163	`(seed * 1_000_003) XOR day`. Exact integer seed and exact actions/configuration
   164	are sufficient; external RNG injection would invalidate the test.
   165	
   166	## Export contract to implement after the native seam lands
   167	
   168	1. At game start, bind a unique evaluation/game ordinal to its actual **resolved
   169	   per-game seed**, resolved configuration, source/engine/schema versions,
   170	   candidate/incumbent checkpoint hashes and seat assignment. Capture the consumed
   171	   seed, not base seed, current `next_seed`, or a guess from environment index.
   172	   Contract v4 consumes seeds at construction and explicit resets, then at
   173	   simultaneous terminal resets in environment-index order.
   174	2. For selected games, retain the exact executed token lengths and tokens, plus
   175	   decoded engine actions in seat order. Decode against the pre-step actor count
   176	   and order limit using the native grammar. STOP terminates the token program;
   177	   it is not an extra game transition. Retain NONE/EMPTY and omitted/explicit
   178	   quantities as native decoding specifies, without a second Python decoder.
   179	3. Preserve list order and insertion order of inventories and shed mappings,
   180	   including zero-valued keys. Do not `sort_keys=True` these payloads. Movement,
   181	   hand indices, ordered market queues, capacity-limited deposits and duplicate
   182	   shop positions make order observable. Use exact JSON integers and round-trip
   183	   float64 money; never regenerate full state from scaled float32 model tensors.
   184	4. Prefer an opt-in evaluation recorder that saves seed/configuration and decoded
   185	   actions, then materializes full snapshots through native seed replay after the
   186	   game. This avoids JSON in ordinary collection. Compare the replay against
   187	   captured initial/terminal snapshots, per-transition banks and any retained
   188	   diagnostic checkpoints; a replay compared only with its own output is circular.
   189	   Exact all-state certification additionally needs captured full snapshots at
   190	   every transition of the selected games (or an independent engine oracle).
   191	   Limit this diagnostic cost to those selected games and measure it separately.
   192	5. Capture terminal evidence **before auto-reset**. The default is 719 transitions,
   193	   720 observations, final step 719, statuses DONE and raw-bank rewards. Contract
   194	   v4's returned terminal-step observation belongs to the new game; terminal
   195	   metrics/banks belong to the completed game. Copy ephemeral evidence before
   196	   the next native call. PPO shaped rewards stay in diagnostics, not Kaggle rewards.
   197	   Artificial truncation is a partial episode, not a fabricated DONE/winner.
   198	6. Serialize Kaggle `steps` with the timing above, `info.seed`, the full supported
   199	   public configuration and pinned schema. Also retain a source-bound seed header
   200	   and action tape for native verification. Native runtime errors or failed
   201	   transactions must produce an explicit incomplete/error record, never a
   202	   successful replay with missing turns. Keep the eight exported selections
   203	   reproducible, including both model-seat assignments where applicable.
   204	
   205	The native replay adapter should reject unsupported v4 configuration, missing
   206	seed, non-integral/negative seed, incorrect action count, nonconsecutive steps,
   207	count mismatch and malformed terminal records with explicit errors. Wider-than-
   208	53-bit seeds must survive JSON/Python/Rust without float conversion. A browser
   209	display is not an authoritative parser for those seeds.
